g, then got a gift on move 16 when White's G4 lost 11.7 points and put Black ahead by 5.8. One move later Black's F3 lost 17.3 points and the lead was gone. After that the lead never came back within single digits, and Black resigned at about 20 points down.", "moments": [{"turn": 9, "text": "Black's D4 dropped the lead from -0.3 to -4.3, a 4.0-point loss. The engine preferred F3. That was the first big slip, and it left Black trailing in the middle of a tight fight."}, {"turn": 16, "text": "White's G4 lost 11.7 points, swinging the lead from -6.0 to +5.8 in Black's favour. The engine's choice was B4. For one move the 10k had given the game away."}, {"turn": 17, "text": "Black's F3 took back that gift, and more. The lead went from +5.8 to -11.6, a 17.3-point loss and the worst move of the game. The engine wanted B3 instead. The game was decided here."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "H4 lost another 8.8 points, taking the lead from -5.2 to -14.0 and making this Black's second blunder. The engine's choice was B3. White's stones were already forming a wall in the centre, and the lead stayed far out of reach for the rest of the game."}, {"turn": 43, "text": "E9 lost 4.4 points, moving the lead from -15.8 to -20.2. In the last stretch both sides traded losses of roughly 4 points a move, so Black stayed around 15 to 20 points behind. White's H8 followed at -19.9, and Black resigned."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses the pasted board and prints each group's liberties, count.py only does an area count of the current position, and the other commands read notes and append to games.md; none of them chooses, scores or looks ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}